  message: "DEPENDENCY NOTE FROM WI-kozaj (2026-10-03, branch jgstern-agent/fix/kozaj, not merged yet). Part 2 of this item's fix is now a ONE-LINE row, no analyzer change: py.py's new _library_producer_type types the result of a call whose import-resolved qualified callee is a key in library_signatures/python.yaml. So `urllib.request.build_opener: urllib.request.OpenerDirector` in that file types `opener` for `import urllib.request; opener = urllib.request.build_opener()`, `from urllib.request import build_opener` and, by the code path tested with `from defusedcsv import csv; csv.writer(f)`, `from urllib import request; request.build_opener()` (a from-imported owner resolves for DECLARED types only; this exact urllib form was not run). Verified on real analyzer output with that exact row supplied through the user channel: test_py_library_producer_types.py::TestAnyRowWorksNotOnlyCsv::test_a_user_row_types_the_receiver gives `opener.open` the module slot urllib.request.OpenerDirector, and the control without the row leaves it on external. Still needed here: the net_send row on urllib.request.OpenerDirector.open, the CATALOGUE_SCOPE entry for urllib.request.OpenerDirector (test_catalogue_scope_gates), and the finding-level A/B the item asks for."  # 6c72
