  message: "WORK DONE 2026-10-03 (concurrent run, stage 4). Branch jgstern-agent/fix/dibit (local, not pushed), base origin/dev fe3c32259d: 31d0dc6e09 fix(catalogue) + ae4ae5cd0b test(python).\n\nCHANGE (YAML + tests, no analyzer change): library_signatures/python.yaml `urllib.request.build_opener: urllib.request.OpenerDirector` (consumed by WI-kozaj's _library_producer_type; `type(urllib.request.build_opener()) is urllib.request.OpenerDirector` checked on 3.12 in a test); io_primitives/python.yaml `urllib.request.OpenerDirector` methods [open, error] net_send (ADR-0059 instance methods; net_send not net_recv, urlopen's reason; `error` re-sends through the redirect/auth handlers and over-approximates the raising case) + a module_completeness entry for the class (4 public methods, introspected: add_handler, close no I/O); CATALOGUE_SCOPE admits the class; survey doc sentence updated; WI-kozaj's user-channel test re-keyed to an unrowed name (its no-row control went red once the row shipped built-in).\n\nBEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE (verify-claims, host_secret -> network, JSON parsed): dev -> branch. `opener = urllib.request.build_opener(); opener.open(url, data=secret)` confirmed_with_caveats -> violated (os.environ -> urllib.request.OpenerDirector.open, ddg confirmed); same for `from urllib.request import build_opener`, `from urllib import request; request.build_opener()`, opener built in caller / sent in callee (ddg_mixed), data in a Request object; hand-built `OpenerDirector()` + add_handler inconclusive -> violated. Controls: urlopen(url, data=secret) violated at urlopen both arms; clean hand-built opener -> confirmed (no caveats), and goes inconclusive \"could not classify (urllib.request.OpenerDirector)\" with the completeness entry removed (mutation run). Tests: red 18 failed / 3 passed without the rows; targeted smart-test 10273 passed, 2 failed (the kozaj control, fixed in ae4ae5cd0b; a hypothesis too_slow health check in tests/test_transcript_pipeline_properties.py, box load) -> rerun of those + the new file 87 passed. mypy ratchet clean.\n\nCORPUS A/B (generic-taint-claims.yaml, 7 claims; A = dev snapshot, B = branch snapshot, each arm printed its tree, per-arm caches): django and superset. Verdict moves: django host-secret-no-network inconclusive(0) -> violated(1), django host-description-no-network inconclusive(0) -> violated(2), superset host-description-no-network inconclusive(0) -> violated(2), superset host-secret-no-network violated(4) -> violated(5). All 6 new flows sink at the two corpus opener.open sites (django templates.py TemplateCommand.download, superset utils/csv.py get_chart_csv_data). Read by hand: 2 are build_opener's OWN env_read reaching the send through the receiver (WI-patit, ruling needed), 4 are approximate cross-function host_description flows (ddg_mixed, cross_function) whose value does not reach the open() arguments (django os.getcwd/expanduser in handle/handle_template; superset datetime.utcnow timing). So: 0 new true findings on the corpus; the measured effect is the fixture false clean closed plus a precision cost. Not run: pytorch (testowners_linter.py:55, the third corpus site), virtualbox (1.4 GB).\n\nRESIDUALS FILED: WI-patit (receiver env-read ruling), WI-tumol (receive half: HTTP response / create_connection socket mint no untrusted_input -- false clean), WI-himij (other stdlib network clients read inconclusive)."  # 4343
